// expect: compile_error
// expect-error: E056

// Calling a constrained generic function with the wrong number of arguments —
// proposal 0185 stage 2 / KI-082.
//
// `describe` takes one argument. The interesting part is *why* this was ever
// accepted: a constrained function is lowered with its dictionaries prepended
// to the parameter list, so arity checking that counted lowered parameters saw
// a band of acceptable counts rather than one number, and a call carrying as
// many extra arguments as the function has dictionaries slipped through — to
// fail at run time as `E1000` instead.
//
// Arity is now checked against the source signature.

fn describe<a: Show>(x: a) -> String {
    show(x)
}

fn main() with IO {
    print(describe(1, 2))
}
